        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Only Two Verbs",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Creation is always fork, clone or posix_spawn",
            "Running a new program is always exec",
            "Nothing else makes a process on Linux"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Call",
            "Returns",
            "Keeps"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "fork",
              "twice",
              "everything, lazily (COW)"
            ],
            [
              "exec",
              "never, on success",
              "the PID only"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "c",
          "lines": [
            "pid_t p = fork();",
            "if (p == 0) {",
            "  execvp(argv[0], argv);",
            "  _exit(127);  // exec failed",
            "}",
            "waitpid(p, &st, 0);"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Under The Hood",
          "items": [
            "==clone()== is the real primitive",
            "Threads = clone sharing memory",
            "posix_spawn = fork+exec in one call"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. The Lifecycle"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "fork",
              "exec",
              "run",
              "exit",
              "zombie",
              "parent waits",
              "gone"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Skip the wait and the zombie stays. That is the whole bug, every time."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "STAT",
            "State"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "R",
              "running"
            ],
            [
              "S",
              "sleeping"
            ],
            [
              "D",
              "**uninterruptible**"
            ],
            [
              "T",
              "stopped"
            ],
            [
              "Z",
              "zombie"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "D Means Wait",
          "text": "In D state even SIGKILL stays pending until the I/O returns."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Four Identity Numbers"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Summary: The Whole Model (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "PID identifies you inside a PID namespace",
            "PPID names your parent",
            "PGID groups a pipeline, SID groups the session",
            "Signals travel along exactly those groupings"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Container sees its entrypoint as ==PID 1==",
            "Host sees that same task as e.g. 24831",
            "One task, two numbers"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Signals In One Breath",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Async notifications with three dispositions",
            "Default, ignore, or your own handler",
            "Standard signals coalesce when blocked",
            "Real-time signals queue and keep their order"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "",
            "Standard",
            "Real-time"
          ],
          "rows": [
