        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "The Uncatchable Pair",
          "text": "SIGKILL and SIGSTOP are the only two signals that cannot be caught, blocked or ignored. Ask first, wait a grace period, then take."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Dead vs Orphaned"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Zombies waste PIDs, never memory",
            "Fix the parent's reaping, not the symptom",
            "Orphans keep running and are adopted",
            "Adopted by PID 1 or the nearest subreaper"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "ps -eo pid,ppid,stat,comm |",
            "  awk '$3 ~ /^Z/'   # zombies",
            "kill -TERM <ppid>   # PID 1 reaps"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Job Control Recap",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "It is signals + process groups + a terminal",
            "Ctrl-C = SIGINT to the foreground group",
            "Ctrl-Z = SIGTSTP to the same group",
            "bg/fg = SIGCONT plus a terminal handoff"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "sleep 300      # Ctrl-Z -> T",
            "bg %1          # SIGCONT, runs",
            "fg %1          # + gets the tty"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Handler Discipline"
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
