    "text": "Part 5 of LINUX PROCESSES & SIGNALS. kill -9 didn't work? The process was in D state, sitting inside the kernel, not reading signals until its disk I/O returned. 14 pages of handwritten notes on how Linux really creates, runs and kills processes: fork returning twice, exec never returning, the zombie you cannot kill, why your container takes exactly 10 seconds to stop, and the full signal catalog. Save it for the next time a daemon won't die.",
